WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.500
The Myers–Briggs Type Indicator&nbsp;
is a self-assessment of how we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.420
perceive the world and make decisions.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:16.500
The test measures our preferences in&nbsp;
4 domains: sources of mental energy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:22.380
processing of information, approach to&nbsp;
decision-making, and need for structure.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:29.820
Each of the four categories has two&nbsp;
sides: extroversion or introversion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:36.840
sensing or intuition, thinking or&nbsp;
feeling, and judging or perceiving.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.460
This then results in 16&nbsp;
possible personality types.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.560
Before we begin the test, keep 3 things in mind:

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:52.140
Human traits exist on a spectrum: you could fall&nbsp;
in the center of two extremes and get different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:57.000
results when repeating the test later.
The MBTI looks at preferences. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.960
people who prefer extraversion over&nbsp;
introversion may not be extraverts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.940
they simply like that personality type better.
Don’t take the results too seriously.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:11.880
To determine your type, ask&nbsp;
yourself these 4 questions.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:19.560
Do you focus outwardly or inwardly?
Are you rather outgoing or private?&nbsp;

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:25.560
Do you speak impulsively or thoughtfully?
Do you get energized being around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:31.920
others or do you recharge alone?
Do you prefer extraversion or introversion??

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:39.900
How do you prefer to take in information?
Do you focus on how things are or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:43.980
imagine how things could be?
Do you pay attention to concrete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:49.680
details or do you see the big picture?
Do you prefer practical ideas or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:54.780
enjoy theories for their own sake?
Do you favor sensing or intuition?

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:02.160
How do you like to make decisions?
Do you rely on logic or personal values?&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:06.840
Do you prioritize fairness and&nbsp;
justice or forgiveness and harmony?&nbsp;

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.760
Do you enjoy finding flaws in&nbsp;
arguments or agreeing with others?&nbsp;

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.700
Do you like thinking or feeling?

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:23.040
How do you prefer to live your outer life?
Do you want matters settled or options open?&nbsp;

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.840
Do you think rules need to be&nbsp;
respected or see them as suggestions?&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:32.280
Do you like detailed instructions&nbsp;
or prefer improvisation?&nbsp;

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.520
Do you like judging or perceiving?

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:43.920
Now that you know who you are, you can take the&nbsp;
letters representing extraversion, introversion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:53.160
sensing, intuition, thinking, feeling, judging,&nbsp;
and perceiving and form your type, say ESTJ.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.420
What that means, becomes clear when&nbsp;
we look at the 16 personality types.

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:10.440
ESTPs enjoy being around people and focus on the&nbsp;
here and now. Their minds are quick, intelligent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:17.340
and outspoken. Good at reading others, they&nbsp;
can solve complex problems. Routines bore them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:22.380
and they see rules as recommendations.
They are often called doers.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:31.200
ESTJs prefer things settled and are not&nbsp;
interested in abstract ideas. They value&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:37.200
security and are also known as guardians.&nbsp;
At work, they are capable of organizing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:41.400
getting things done, and are loyal&nbsp;
colleagues who don’t miss small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:47.100
important details. To keep things neat,&nbsp;
they want everyone to follow the protocol.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:56.520
ESFPs are friendly, social, and accepting.&nbsp;
They love to have new experiences and meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.520 --> 00:04:03.060
new people. ESPFs enjoy seeing others happy and&nbsp;
as a result, are often the center of attention.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:10.020
Disliking analysis, they have plenty of common&nbsp;
sense. Instead of logic, they are driven by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:15.960
values and hence tend to agree with people&nbsp;
they like. They are also called performers.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:25.740
ESFJs are warm-hearted and cooperative. They&nbsp;
feel a strong sense of duty, value traditions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:31.740
and are loyal friends. At work, they are&nbsp;
detailed and tend to complete tasks accurately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:37.320
and on time. Their empathy allows them to&nbsp;
see what others need, which makes them good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:43.860
leaders. ESFJs want to be appreciated for&nbsp;
who they are and are known as caregivers.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:53.040
ENFPs are known as enthusiastic idealists&nbsp;
who see a life full of possibilities. Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:58.080
minds are spontaneous, creative, and are&nbsp;
able to do almost anything that interests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.840
them — although the affirmation of their peers&nbsp;
greatly influences their behavior. At work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:08.940
ENFPs are fast thinkers, and good&nbsp;
at improvising. But they do get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:14.040
bored with details or things they don’t&nbsp;
care about. Some call them inspirers.

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:23.460
ENFJs are warm, responsive, and able to take&nbsp;
responsibility. They show outstanding people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:29.700
skills and see plenty of potential in others.&nbsp;
This makes them good managers and inspiring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:36.120
leaders. Since they are concerned about how others&nbsp;
think and feel, they are also known as givers.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:45.060
ENTPs are intellectually quick, creative,&nbsp;
and good at a broad range of things. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:50.580
get excited about new projects but are so&nbsp;
bored by routines that they rarely do the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:55.800
same thing the same way. Their ability&nbsp;
to read others, think strategically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:01.920
and solve complex problems, makes them&nbsp;
stimulating friends. Some call them visionaries.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:11.340
ENTJs tend to be confident, frank, and quick&nbsp;
to make a decision. They value competence and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:17.280
have no patience for nonsense. At work, they&nbsp;
are quick to spot poor organizational design&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:22.680
and are able to create intelligent new&nbsp;
solutions. They like to make long-term&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:28.800
plans and then implement them no matter what.&nbsp;
That’s one reason some call them executives.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:34.260
And now those who prefer introverts.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:40.860
ISTJs are calm, serious, and interested&nbsp;
in peaceful living. Their judgment is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:44.340
thorough and realistic. They&nbsp;
like to keep things organized,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:48.240
are hardworking, and are focused&nbsp;
on achieving what they set out to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:54.600
The fact that they are loyal, reliable, and&nbsp;
detailed gave them the nickname inspectors.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:03.900
ISTPs are reserved and relaxed until there is&nbsp;
a problem. Then, they act quickly and usually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:10.260
find a good solution. Their curiosity about&nbsp;
how things work makes them good analysts and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:16.200
great engineers. Their thinking is structured&nbsp;
and logical, but not afraid to break the rules&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:21.540
if they get in the way of them doing something&nbsp;
extraordinary. They are known as the mechanics.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:31.380
ISFJs are introverts that are conscientious and&nbsp;
kind. They often have a high degree of empathy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:36.900
remember specifics about their friends. At work,&nbsp;
they are committed to meeting their obligations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:43.500
and like to see everyone happy. Interested&nbsp;
in serving others, they are called nurturers.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:52.980
ISFPs are serious, sensitive, and good-hearted.&nbsp;
They are very loyal friends and committed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:59.040
their personal values. Conflicts stress them out,&nbsp;
which is why they don’t like to lead or control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:05.340
others. Their sense of time and appreciation&nbsp;
for beauty gave them the alias artists.

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:15.660
INFJs are sensitive, original, and the rarest of&nbsp;
all types. Their strong intuition means that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:21.960
trust their instincts above all else. They prefer&nbsp;
neither leading nor following but doing what feels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:27.660
right. Their devotion to protecting what they&nbsp;
value earned them the pseudonym defenders.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:37.740
INFPs are reflective, loyal, and often idealistic.&nbsp;
Their primary goal is to find out their meaning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:43.800
in life — to make the world a better place. At&nbsp;
work, they like to help and are quick to spot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:51.120
possibilities to make things better. Interested in&nbsp;
serving humanity, they are also called idealists.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:09:01.020
INTJs have minds that are original, independent,&nbsp;
and analytical. At work, they think long-term,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:07.200
are determined, and show a high standard of&nbsp;
competence - for themselves and others. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:13.680
makes them natural leaders. Their knowledge and&nbsp;
cognitive ability gave them the alias scientists.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:23.820
INTPs are creative and rational and get excited&nbsp;
about theories and ideas. Their tendency to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:29.100
quiet makes them hard to read. Although when&nbsp;
they focus on problems they find interesting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:33.000
they often reveal their true&nbsp;
character. They have natural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:39.000
skepticism and logical explanations for&nbsp;
almost everything. They are called thinkers.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:47.460
The building blocks of the original MBTI were&nbsp;
laid by Katharine Briggs and her daughter Isabel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:54.660
Briggs Myers who based their work on Carl Jung’s&nbsp;
`influential 1921 theory of psychological types’.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:01.620
What do you think? Can we&nbsp;
divide individuals into 2, 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:07.980
8 or 16 personality types and then infer&nbsp;
who they are? Share your thoughts in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:13.560
